# HEX ONLY (read-safe). Decodes to the SAFE tui-showcase: an HONEST, self-labeling,
# DISPLAY-ONLY educational board. Cat'd in a traditional terminal it paints a full-screen
# "WHAT YOU SEE vs WHAT IS THERE" table where every row NAMES a text-attack class and
# shows a LIVE example, so plain cat hides the trick and a safe tool reveals it. It
# changes only the DISPLAY: the alternate screen (?1049h), which `reset` restores, and the
# window title (OSC 0), which `reset` does NOT restore -- clear it with `printf '\033]0;\007'`.
# It does NOT touch the clipboard, type at the prompt, or run
# anything. Live display classes: homoglyph (Cyrillic + Greek), ASCII look-alike, bidi
# (U+202E), zero-width (U+200B), BOM (U+FEFF), combining/Zalgo, fullwidth (U+FF2x),
# control-byte CR+erase, hidden-by-colour (SGR), DEC charset shift, OSC 8 hyperlink,
# OSC 0 title, CSI ?1049h alt-screen, and honest Greek as the NON-attack contrast.
# Classes that reach OUTSIDE the display -- clipboard (OSC 52), input reflection (DSR /
# answerback), notification (OSC 9) and the reflected-command RCE -- are NOT in this file;
# they are fired + conformance-tested live in the SANDBOX by their own PoCs and compared
# on secure-terminal.github.io. Viewing THIS hex never fires anything (SAFETY.md); run the
# decoded file only in a throwaway terminal and 'reset' after.
